WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Hello everybody! My name is Markiplier

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.260
and welcome to Minecraft.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.320
Now I know it's been a long time since the last time I played this game

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.240
but that's kind of a good thing

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.880
because there's been an incredible number of updates to the game

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.920
like, eleven full updates to the game since the last time I played it.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.380
So, I thought the best way to get into this

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.620
Uh, which is going to be a very long term series

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.760
I'm probably gonna do, maybe 100 parts of this before I'll get through all the new stuff,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.660
but I thought the best place to start

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.920
would be to just create a new world

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.800
call it what I wanna call it

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.360
I'll call it "Markiplier's Fun House"

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.540
And then just get into it

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.500
and start exploring from the ground up.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.720
Because sometimes you just gotta get your hands dirty when you're playing a new game

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.160
and really start fresh

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.820
because what you think you know, can get in the way of what you will discover

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.760
in the world.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.280
So

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.160
I uuh...

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.360
Man it's been a while since I played this

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.520
It's been a while since I've been back in the Minecraft world and...

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.740
Ya know I gotta say it's good to be back

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.600
It's good to be uhh...

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.060
It's good to be back into this whole environment

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.500
And one of the things that I like the most about Minecraft

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.900
has always been the music and the sound and the ambiance

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.100
because where it doesn't have graphics

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.140
is where it might

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.000
have some more experience to discover

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.860
And as usual, this hasn't changed.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.640
I know you guys are wondering like,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.320
"Ah man, is the very basic building blocks of the game different?"

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.880
The answer is nooo

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:23.560
*heh*

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.140
And uh..

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.940
You still punch wood to get it

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.440
I don't know, I don't know

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.740
It's charming at this point

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.740
Just the fact that you're slamming your bony fists into a hunk of wood

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.400
And hoping that

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.160
it'll - It'll -it'll

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.860
smash to pieces before your.. your brittle skeleton does

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.660
But you know

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.400
You just do what you can with what you got

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.700
And if you've forgotten

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.120
Oh, there's my little guy

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.280
I still get an achievement for taking inventory

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.860
But, it's, it's all the same

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.720
You just craft up a storm

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.220
Oh

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.160
Man I'm getting ahead of myself

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.700
I totally forgot how to play

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.300
You gotta make wood first ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.060
And then make a table out of that!

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.440
because, once you have the crafting table

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.900
You're still able to make all of the other basic fundamental building blocks

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.940
of this entire game.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.780
Because it starts from the very

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.500
You know

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.280
Early stages of what you're supposed to do

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.400
And then grows

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.640
Into something even bigger and better

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.140
Now

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.280
You may be seeing

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.600
I don't know what thi-i-iis is *glitching*

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.900
Is this a shield *glitch* or something? I have no idea

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.400
*glitching* No idea, n-n-no idea

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.640
*muffled* -weird, I don't even know where to being with this stuff

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.960
*computer screeching*

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.700
*infinite blue screen*

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.180
*start-up sounds*

